OL,3,GNEWSAPara-snooker player missed flight
OL,4,Aover hoist issue
OL,5,
OL,6,FA para-snooker player who was refused
OL,7,Faccess to his flight at the last minute
OL,8,Fbecause his hoist was too heavy says
OL,9,Fdisabled people are being treated like
OL,10,F"second-class citizens" by airlines.
OL,12,FMatthew Lester missed his flight to
OL,13,FBulgaria for the World Disability
OL,14,FBilliards and Snooker European
OL,15,FChampionship, despite notifying carrier
OL,16,FWizz Air in advance of the equipment he
OL,17,Fwould be travelling with.
OL,19,FHe said: "It's just astounding to me
OL,20,Fthat in this day and age disabled
OL,21,Fpeople get treated like second class
OL,22,Fcitizens by airlines."
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,389,380,200,160,0,100
